     This is a minor Catch-22 which should get fixed--or at least improved--
in the next update.  NetHack is trying to tell you that it doesn't know
what i/o interface to use, but since it doesn't know what i/o interface,
it's unable to tell you...

     You probably redefined DEFAULT_WINDOW_SYS to "X11" without also
defining X11_GRAPHICS.  In that case, there's no X11 code present to handle
the output.  Restore the default to "tty", or #define X11_GRAPHICS, or both.


